<!--
  RSW_CanopySwinger.xml                  SWBestiary - COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug `the_greentide:canopy-swinger`
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_greentide.md §4: "The Swingers —
  nimble canopy dwellers crossing above the river to escape danger… or
  falling into it (owner)"; roster's own `new_defs` entry,
  rosters/the_greentide.json, mechanic_load "none blocking (falls into
  water as flavor)").

  Checked cast_assignment.csv first (per this item's own "watch out"): no
  existing row is tagged a "swinger"/canopy-prey band anywhere in the
  greentide cast — `Kinrath` (row 184) is the canopy-AMBUSH PREDATOR the
  sheet itself calls out as preying on Swingers, a separate niche, already
  kept there. The nearest reusable body is `RSW_KowakianMonkeyLizard`
  (already ported, MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave C) — a bipedal arboreal
  primate-lizard, canonically agile and jungle-native — and it is NOT wired
  into any RUT_ biome's wildAnimals (checked: only appears in the
  auto-generated cross-cutting AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Generated.xml /
  AnimalTolerances_Ashkarr.xml patches, never a per-biome wildAnimals list),
  so reusing its body/art asset here does not double-book the species — the
  donor row `KowakianMonkeyLizard` (bare, arid_shrubland "small-runway",
  cast_assignment.csv row 42) is a DIFFERENT tracked entity from our own
  `RSW_` port, same asset-reuse-without-species-reuse pattern
  RSW_TunnelSnake (reusing RSW_Klorslug) and RSW_VentStalker (reusing
  RSW_Kinrath) used.

  Mechanism: "falls into water as flavor" needs no bespoke C# — an ordinary
  arboreal-reading grazer/omnivore with no aquatic comp, matching the
  roster's own "none blocking" tag exactly; the fall-into-the-river beat is
  prose, not a mechanic (no swim comp exists in this codebase to hook it
  to). MoveSpeed raised from the donor's 4.0 to 5.5 and Wildness raised from
  0.40 to 0.6 (a true wild canopy animal, not the donor's exotic-pet
  framing) to read "nimble" and "escapes danger" as real stats. Herd size
  widened (the sheet's own "crossing above the river" reads as troops, not
  loners).

  Art: zero new PNGs — same texPath as RSW_KowakianMonkeyLizard
  (swanimals/KowakianMonkeyLizard/...), retinted at the def level only via
  flavor text, not a new render (checked infrastructure/artpipe/
  {done,pending,registry.jsonl} for "canopyswinger"/"swinger" first — clean,
  confirming no prior job exists for this subject; none filed here either,
  since the asset-reuse posture ships with zero new art by design, same as
  RSW_TunnelSnake/RSW_VentStalker).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase" ADogSaidBody="LegsTail">
    <defName>RSW_CanopySwinger</defName>
    <label>canopy swinger</label>
    <description>A lean, long-limbed climber that never touches the ground if it can help it, crossing the gaps between the Greentide's giants hand over hand along vine and branch. When the canopy runs out — or something faster is behind it — it simply lets go, trusting the river below to break the fall better than whatever is chasing it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>5.5</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>90</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Wildness>0.6</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
